# use-apfel-mcp

Token-efficient reading and tool routing for tight/on-device (~4096-token) budgets.

## Preprocess before reading raw

If a code file, log, or doc/URL content is going to land in context and it's more than ~1-2k chars, don't read it whole — pipe it through the matching script in `scripts/` (resolve relative to this rule's own directory, e.g. `~/.agents/skills/use-apfel-mcp/scripts/` if installed via the standard path):

| Input | Tool | Effect |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Code/JSON file | `scripts/ast-skeleton.py` | Signatures/exports/deps only (~150 tokens) |
| Log/build output | `scripts/log-filter.py` | Deduped errors, warnings, final status, timeline |
| Long doc/article | `scripts/relevance-rank.py "<query>"` | Top 3 paragraphs matching the query, scored |

Skip when content is already short, or you need an exact-line edit (a skeleton drops line numbers/bodies).

## Full reference

See [SKILL.md](../../SKILL.md) in this repo for the complete apfel-mcp tool-routing table, hard call-count/output-cap rules, and `apfel-mcp-fs` caveats (read-only, 6k-char cap, allowlisted).
